  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The droplets' paths and the bow of the stream, the tether's wobble and the brand change per cast. The drain length stays fixed."
  },
  "director_notes": "Vampire line, a blood drain. The flow must read as coming back to the caster, so the blood is sparks anchored at the target with home_to: caster_hand (new): each drop bursts out of the victim and is pulled to the hand, arriving as it dies, with a seeded bow so the stream isn't one straight line. The tether is a thin water-style beam in blood colours. The orb in the hand grows by keyframes as the drain runs, then pops into a flash and a ring at sate."
